WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.386
Begin with one shared clock.

2
00:00:02.386 --> 00:00:05.237
The host launches work, the GPU executes

3
00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:08.494
it, and the host eventually receives the
result.

4
00:00:08.494 --> 00:00:10.123
This timeline is schematic.

5
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:17.123
While the GPU computes, the host can be
waiting for that same work.

6
00:00:17.123 --> 00:00:19.693
Adding both durations double counts
overlapping time.

7
00:00:19.693 --> 00:00:21.529
Read the two lanes together.

8
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:29.725
In the saved mixed-backend profile, FP64
share correction accounts for about

9
00:00:29.725 --> 00:00:32.657
sixty-four percent of recorded GPU
activity.

10
00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:35.589
This is not a wall-time percentage.

11
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.863
That hotspot tells us where to inspect

12
00:00:38.863 --> 00:00:40.658
launches, arithmetic and intermediate
memory.

13
00:00:40.658 --> 00:00:44.606
It does not say that all its time can be
removed.

14
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.672
Change one implementation detail, validate

15
00:00:50.672 --> 00:00:53.922
the complete answer, then repeat clean
timings.

16
00:00:53.922 --> 00:00:56.244
The profile guides the experiment.

17
00:00:56.244 --> 00:00:59.495
Unprofiled complete runs determine whether
it helped.
